  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "transferBadPixelsToMap",
    "file": "librawspeed/src/librawspeed/common/RawImage.cpp",
    "description": "RawImageData::transferBadPixelsToMap() trusts entries in mBadPixelPositions and only guards them with assert(pos_x < uncropped_dim.x) / assert(pos_y < uncropped_dim.y). For this PoV, malformed decode state produces at least one bad-pixel coordinate outside uncropped_dim, so the debug assertion aborts instead of handling/rejecting invalid coordinates. Root cause is missing runtime validation/sanitization of bad-pixel coordinates before indexing/bit-setting in the bad-pixel map.",
    "conditions": "In the TIFF/DNG fuzz harness, attacker-controlled file metadata/content flows through decodeRawInternal into RawImage state, including bad pixel positions. When decodeRaw() calls raw->fixBadPixels() (RawDecoder.cpp), transferBadPixelsToMap() iterates those positions. If any encoded position has x or y >= uncropped image dimensions, the assert in RawImage.cpp:319-320 fires (ASan ABRT). Trigger requires interpolateBadPixels path enabled (as in this harness) and crafted input that injects out-of-range bad pixel coordinates."
  },
